<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
The launcher icon: the mark the desktop window already wears, on white.

Three layers, because Android draws three. `background` is a flat colour
so every launcher mask — circle, squircle, teardrop — cuts a clean edge;
`foreground` is the mark itself, drawn at 58% of the 108dp canvas so it
sits inside the 66dp circle every launcher promises to show, whatever it
does with the corners; `monochrome` is the same silhouette for themed
icons, where the system supplies the colour and only the alpha is read.

The white is stated here rather than taken from the palette: a launcher
draws this in its own process and its own configuration, and an icon that
changed with the phone's theme would stop being the thing people look for.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/gilune_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
